# Skill registry

When a customer request matches a skill, read and follow that skill before acting. Mention the relevant option conversationally when it could be useful.

- **`init-local-ticket-branch`:** Use when starting implementation for an `ECOMM-*` ticket or a NOTICKET branch. Follow ticket branch naming and Jira transition rules.
- **`commit-it-then`:** Use for commits. Keep conventional type, ticket suffix (`[ECOMM-*]` or `[NOTICKET]`), and subject length requirements.
- **`open-github-pr`:** Use when the customer wants a PR. Read the repository PR template, fill it, and create the PR only after approval.
- **`clean-up-current-branch`:** Use when the customer wants to stash current work, switch to `main`, and delete the previous local branch. Do not run on `main` or `master`.
- **`cleanup-zb-agent-docker`:** Use when the customer wants to clear running Docker containers. Warn that it affects every running container on the machine.
- **`generate-timesheet`:** Use for Jira timesheets, weekly reports, status updates, or "what I worked on" summaries.
- **`zenapi-pr-dependency-safety`:** Use for zenapi dependency PR safety reviews.

Do not invoke cleanup, branch creation, commits, pushes, or PR creation silently. Ask first unless the current customer message explicitly approves that specific action.
